# SPA fallback: every path boots the Blazor router, which renders its own
# NotFound UI for unknown addresses. The tradeoff is that unknown paths
# return 200 instead of 404. Search engines call that a soft 404.
# Workers Static Assets cannot tell valid client routes (/history, /plan)
# from invalid ones without a Worker script router, so a 404 rewrite would
# return 404 for valid deep links too. 404.html mirrors index.html so
# removing this rule later still renders the app shell with a 404 status.
# (assets.notFoundHandling single-page-application in cloudflare.config.ts
# provides the same fallback at the routing layer.)
/* /index.html 200
